{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Hermitian structure of the transfer matrices, abstractly\n\nThe question: do the $t_a$ commute with their Hermitian conjugates, when everything is written in terms of generators with $E_{ij}^\\dagger=E_{ji}$ (the EH convention)? Everything here is abstract, with no representation:\n- **Algebra.** Generators `gen[s,i,j]` $=E^{(s)}_{ij}$ satisfy $[E_{ij},E_{kl}]=\\delta_{jk}E_{il}-\\delta_{li}E_{kj}$ on each site, and different sites commute. Words `nc[...]` are normal-ordered by (site, $i$, $j$).\n- **Conjugation.** $\\dagger$ reverses products, maps $E^{(s)}_{ij}\\to E^{(s)}_{ji}$, and conjugates scalars. The conjugates are separate symbols ($u\\to\\bar u$ = `ub`, $\\theta_s\\to$ `θb[s]`, $h\\to$ `hb`, $z_i\\to$ `zb[i]`), so any reality conditions show up explicitly.\n- **Conventions** (new). The Lax is $\\mathcal L^{(s)}_{ij}(x)=x\\,\\delta_{ij}+h\\,E^{(s)}_{ij}$, and $T(u)=\\mathcal L^{(1)}(u-\\theta_1)\\cdots\\mathcal L^{(L)}(u-\\theta_L)$ (product in auxiliary space). The twist is diagonal on the right, $T^z_{ij}=T_{ij}z_j$. The quantum minor $\\mathrm{qmin}_{ij,ij}(u)=T_{ii}(u)T_{jj}(u-h)-T_{ji}(u)T_{ij}(u-h)$ gives $t_1=\\sum_iz_iT_{ii}$ and $t_2=\\sum_{i<j}z_iz_j\\,\\mathrm{qmin}_{ij,ij}$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n(* normal ordering of words: order generators by (site, i, j); swapping two out of order costs their commutator (zero across sites) *)\nord[gen[s_, i_, j_]] := {s, i, j};\ncommGen[gen[s_, i_, j_], gen[s_, k_, l_]] := KroneckerDelta[j, k] nc[gen[s, i, l]] - KroneckerDelta[l, i] nc[gen[s, k, j]];\ncommGen[gen[_, __], gen[_, __]] := 0;\nsubWord[nc[a___], nc[m___], nc[b___]] := nc[a, m, b];\nsubWord[nc[a___], c_ nc[m___], nc[b___]] := c nc[a, m, b];\nsubWord[nc[a___], x_Plus, nc[b___]] := subWord[nc[a], #, nc[b]] & /@ x;\nsubWord[_, 0, _] := 0;\nnormal[e_] := Expand[Expand[e] //. nc[a___, x_gen, y_gen, b___] /; OrderedQ[{ord[y], ord[x]}] && ord[x] =!= ord[y] :> nc[a, y, x, b] + subWord[nc[a], commGen[x, y], nc[b]]];\n(* noncommutative product of linear combinations of words *)\nterms[e_] := With[{ee = Expand[e]}, If[Head[ee] === Plus, List @@ ee, {ee}]];\nsplitT[t_] := With[{w = First[Cases[{t}, _nc, Infinity, 1]]}, {t/w, w}];\nncMul[x_, y_] := normal[Total[Flatten[Table[With[{p = splitT[a], q = splitT[b]}, p[[1]] q[[1]] Join[p[[2]], q[[2]]]], {a, DeleteCases[terms[x], 0]}, {b, DeleteCases[terms[y], 0]}]]]];\ncomm[x_, y_] := normal[ncMul[x, y] - ncMul[y, x]];\n(* Hermitian conjugation: reverse words, E_ij -> E_ji, conjugate scalars *)\nconjRules = {u -> ub, v -> vb, h -> hb, θ[s_] :> θb[s], z[i_] :> zb[i]};\ndag[e_] := normal[(e /. conjRules) /. nc[w___] :> (nc @@ (Reverse[{w}] /. gen[s_, i_, j_] :> gen[s, j, i]))];\n(* sanity: the gl(3) relations close and dag is an anti-involution on a product *)\ntestA = nc[gen[1, 1, 2]]; testB = nc[gen[1, 2, 3]];\n{comm[testA, testB], normal[dag[ncMul[testA, testB]] - ncMul[dag[testB], dag[testA]]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<details class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer\">4 warnings</summary><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">ClearAll::wrsym: Symbol ClearGlobals is Protected.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">ClearAll::wrsym: Symbol VsCodeCleanupImgDir is Protected.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">ClearAll::wrsym: Symbol VsCodeDynExportValue is Protected.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">General::stop: Further output of ClearAll::wrsym will be suppressed during this calculation.</div></details>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
