   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. Conjugation: $t_a^\\dagger$ versus $t_a$ at conjugated parameters\nWrite $\\bar t_a(u)$ for $t_a$ with every scalar conjugated, $\\bar t_a(u)=t_a(u)\\big|_{u\\to\\bar u,\\,\\theta\\to\\bar\\theta,\\,h\\to\\bar h,\\,z\\to\\bar z}$. The table shows $\\Delta_a=t_a(u)^\\dagger-\\bar t_a(u)$ word by word, with factored coefficients. If $\\Delta_a=0$, then $t_a^\\dagger$ lies in the same commutative family, provided the conjugated parameters do.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* group a normal-ordered expression by word, factor the coefficients *)\nwordTable[e_] := With[{ws = Union[Cases[{Expand[e]}, _nc, Infinity]]}, Grid[Prepend[Table[{w, Factor[Coefficient[Expand[e], w]]}, {w, ws}], {\"word\", \"coefficient\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]];\nΔ[a_, L_] := Δ[a, L] = normal[dag[If[a == 1, t1[L][u], t2[L][u]]] - (If[a == 1, t1[L][u], t2[L][u]] /. conjRules)];\nGrid[Table[{Row[{\"Δ\", a, \", L=\", L}], If[Δ[a, L] === 0, 0, wordTable[Δ[a, L]]]}, {L, 1, 2}, {a, 1, 2}] // Flatten[#, 1] &, Frame -> All, Alignment -> {Left, Top}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
